# !! DELIBERATELY NOT LISTED HERE: functions/runtime-env.json !!
# It must NOT be in .gitignore. The Firebase CLI honours .gitignore when
# packaging a deploy, so listing it here would exclude it from the deployment
# artifact and silently disable ALL outbound email (every send then no-ops
# with "RESEND_API_KEY is not set").
# It is instead ignored via .git/info/exclude: git honours that file, the
# Firebase CLI does not read it. Verified empirically -- email worked only
# while the file was absent from .gitignore.
#
# This is local-only, so the key is portable-unsafe on a fresh clone. The
# correct fix is Secret Manager + defineSecret (requires enabling
# secretmanager.googleapis.com, currently disabled -> 403).

# One-off scratch scripts and generated release summaries.
/fix-admin.mjs
/mpt_agent.py
/SBConnect-Release-Summary.pdf

# Resend key now lives in Secret Manager (defineSecret), not in a repo file.
# Kept as a safety net so a stray copy can never be committed.
/functions/runtime-env.json
